{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789231723,"nonce":"/cmtNuaKKThDQOcpZ0ra0enJBvY=","title":"A block-bodied if as a function's tail value returns undef","message":"def pick(flag: bool): Any { if flag { 7 } else { \"fallback\" } }\n\nlowers to a CondBranch whose arms end in plain branches to a merge\nblock that returns an undef constant; the arms' values are never\njoined. The typed-AST If *expression* path builds the phi correctly,\nso this is the statement-as-tail-value path, where the parser leaves\nthe node typed Unknown and nothing turns the last statement of each\narm into the block's value.\n\nSame shape with a concrete return type: `def pick(flag: bool): i64 {\nif flag { 7 } else { 8 } }`.","files":null}]}